{"format":1,"key":"zone:darkshore","path":"/lore/zone/darkshore","name":"Darkshore","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"darkshore","name":"Darkshore","path":"/lore/zone/darkshore"},"levels":"Levels 10-20","description":"Darkshore is a cold, mist-shrouded strip of coast lining northwestern Kalimdor, dotted with ancient Kaldorei ruins and troubled wildlife. Anchored by the…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:darkshore","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Darkshore is a cold, mist-shrouded strip of coast lining northwestern Kalimdor, dotted with ancient Kaldorei ruins and troubled wildlife. Anchored by the Alliance harbor town of Auberdine, it serves as the primary continental gateway for travelers arriving from Teldrassil and the Eastern Kingdoms. Beyond the patrolled road, demonic cults, encroaching naga, and a creeping corruption from the highlands threaten the region's delicate balance.","Stretching beneath the western shadows of Mount Hyjal and Felwood, Darkshore is characterized by pine groves, sea fog, and rocky beaches beaten by cold waves. Millennia ago, this coast was home to the flourishing Kaldorei twin cities of Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran. Shattered during the Great Sundering, their skeletal pillars and marble arches now lie half-drowned in the surf or overgrown with roots, haunted by restless Highborne spirits and overrun by scavenger murlocs and invasive naga."],"hash":"3b8af3","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"5e4770bee3","sec":57},"female-narrator":{"sha":"fe0ca9e2b0","sec":59}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Darkshore (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Darkshore_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Darkshore","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Darkshore"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/auberdine","n":"Auberdine","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/ameth-aran","n":"Ameth'Aran","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/master-s-glaive","n":"Master's Glaive","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/quest/952-grove-of-th